<title>USA: Spain's Repsol leads NYSE most-active list.</title>
<headline>Spain's Repsol leads NYSE most-active list.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Repsol SA was the most active issue on the New York Stock Exchange early Tuesday afternoon, with activity boosted by privatization prospects for the Spanish oil group.</p>
<p>Repsol's American Depositary Receipts rose 1/4 to 38-1/8. Volume was 7.6 million shares, topping the most active list.</p>
<p>&quot;The Spanish market has been strong, and they are going to be privatizing the last tranche (of the company) in the next three months. That's what is helping it,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>The Spanish government has said it will sell 10 percent of Repsol and at least 15 percent of electricity company Empresa Nacional de Electricidad, or Endesa, as part of its sell-off of state companies.</p>
<p>Endesa's ADRs were up 1-1/2 at 70-1/8.</p>
<p>((Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
